        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0672" n="1632" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1632"/>

                <head>No. 1112.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cardwell to Mr. Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Agency and Consulate-General of the United States of
                                America</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cairo,
                            Egypt</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-03-10"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March</hi> 10, 1888</date>. (Received April
                        2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 212.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Having made reference more than once to the
                    importance of the American missions in Egypt as an educating agency, and to the
                    propriety of extending this interest the most perfect protection, I beg-to call
                    your attention to a publication, herewith inclosed, which demonstrates its
                    importance and magnitude.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Cardwell</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d399-a1.xml" xpointer="d399-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
